      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Soaking in warm salt water and applying antibiotic ointment is better than the previous suggestions, but this is still a makeshift solution for a deep puncture. The most important next step is to monitor the wound very closely for any signs of spreading infection, such as increased redness, swelling, or pus. Please make a firm plan to visit a medical professional as soon as your work allows, as deep punctures require professional assessment.",
      "source": "target",
